Container-Only Software
================================================================================

The runtime container adds an Azul Zulu build of OpenJDK and Debian operating-
system/font packages that are not part of the executable GridGrind JAR. Their
licenses are not represented by a single GridGrind license expression. The
image retains the JRE legal directory and readme.txt under JAVA_HOME and
package copyright files under /usr/share/doc. GridGrind-specific legal files
are copied to /usr/share/doc/gridgrind. The release workflow attaches
provenance and an SBOM for the image contents.

The corresponding release's Dockerfile identifies the exact official
azul-zulu JRE variant and manifest-list digest. The runtime uses Debian 13;
the contributor container has a separate base and distribution scope.

Base-image definitions and upstream legal/source materials:

https://github.com/AzulSystems/azul-zulu-images
https://docs.azul.com/core/tpl
https://www.azul.com/products/core/openjdk-terms-of-use/
https://sources.debian.org/
https://snapshot.debian.org/

The JRE readme.txt retains Azul's written offer for its OpenJDK-derived
portions, including the source-request address and build-specific version
code. Debian package copyright files identify package-specific terms;
the image SBOM and package metadata identify the installed versions.

Build and fuzz tools, including JQF, are resolved separately by Gradle and are
not bundled in the product JAR, launcher archives or final runtime image.
Those tools are governed by their upstream licenses; this notice does not
relicense them as GridGrind software.

GridGrind makes no separate written source-code offer for third-party
container components. Retained vendor materials and source pointers do not
by themselves establish fulfillment of every redistributor's source-delivery
obligations. Those obligations depend on the actual components and method of
distribution; the upstream offers must not be represented as a new GridGrind
promise.

